    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0716" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/470</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-11">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>737. The Danish Minister here has advised the Department that Mr.
                        Clan, chief of the commercial department of the Danish
                    Ministry of Foreign Affairs, has been sent to London in connection with the
                    general question of the foreign trade of Denmark. It appears <pb facs="0717"
                        n="403" xml:id="pg403"/> that Great Britain desires that Denmark adopt the
                    same system used by Holland in regard to cargoes destined to that country. The
                    Danish Government desires to have Mr. Clan discuss these
                    matters with you in London. Please communicate this to Consul General Skinner, and you are both authorized to enter
                    into informal discussions with Mr. Clan in regard to these
                    matters so far as they affect American trade.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
